# Accepted gaps for 26-namespace-object-fallback — each line is an edge the TypeScript
# compiler resolves and this engine does not. A NEW missing edge fails the suite; a line
# here that STARTS working also fails, so the debt cannot rot.
#
# Both are the SAME gap, and it is not the one this case fixes: a function value bound to
# a name is not found as a callable member (#229), so neither namespace export resolves.
# What this case pins is that the unresolved lookup no longer FALLS BACK to the global
# Object member of the same name. `a()` was answered with `Object#toString` from the
# standard library, which the compiler contradicts; it is now a declared unknown.
#
# `c()` is the control and must keep resolving to Object#toString: that namespace
# declares no `toString`, so Object's really is the right target. If a future change
# suppresses the fallback by asking whether the receiver is a namespace rather than
# whether the scope declares the name, `c()` breaks and this case says so.
caller#a() -> helper#toString(string)
caller#b() -> helper#unique(string)
